use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/Disclosure import Disclosure
from ../../../behaviors/Presence import Presence

export ui-component Collapsible:
    description:
        A collapsible is one section of content that the user can show and hide
        with a button, such as "Show details" under a summary. It tucks
        something away without taking the user anywhere else.

    behaviors:
        - @{Disclosure}
        - @{Presence}

    trigger:
        The button stays where it is whether the section is shown or hidden. It
        tells assistive tools whether the section is shown, and which section
        it controls. Its label can stay the same or change, such as from "Show
        more" to "Show less"; the component decides.

    activation:
        Pressing the trigger the usual way for the platform shows the section
        if it is hidden, and hides it if it is shown. Focus stays on the
        trigger either way.

    state:
        The component decides whether the section starts shown or hidden, and
        can show or hide it itself. It is told each time the user does.

    disabled:
        A disabled collapsible can't be shown or hidden by the user. It stays
        in whichever state it was in.

    direction:
        Usually the section grows and shrinks downwards. It can also grow
        sideways, such as a side panel that folds away.

    partialCollapse:
        The component can keep part of the content showing while collapsed,
        such as the first few lines of a long description, instead of hiding
        all of it. Whether the part that is cut off can still be reached by
        keyboard and assistive tools is up to the chosen library, so it is best
        not to put links or buttons there.

    nonGoals:
        - Not for several sections where opening one may close another. That's
            an Accordion
        - The section doesn't float above the page. A panel that does is a
            Popover
